{"availability":"available","full":"rse/studio-canvas","name":"studio-canvas","description":"Real-Time Virtual Studio Canvas Rendering","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":16,"forks":1,"created":"2023-02-16T19:13:06Z","updated":"2025-08-31T11:43:38Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://github.com/rse/studio-canvas/","topics":["canvas","game-engine-3d","real-time-rendering","scene","studio"],"demo":"https://playground.babylonjs.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:05:38.474Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T19:05:38.474Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T19:05:38.474Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T13:20:18.443Z","stars":16,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-12T19:05:38.474Z","stars":16,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Studio-Canvas is a client/server applications for dynamically rendering the virtual canvas of a filmstudio through the help of a game engine. The canvas optionally is overlayed with a standalone monitor and/or an embedded decal, both showing an own video stream. The virtual cameras optionally can follow the physical PTZ cameras throught their emitted FreeD information.","The application, written in TypeScript, consists of a central Node.js-based server component and a HTML5 Single-Page Application (SPA) as the client component. The client component it turn runs in two distinct modes: a Vue.js based control mode for real-time adjusting the scene parameters and a rendering mode for real-time rendering the scene with the help of the Babylon.js game engine."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rse/studio-canvas/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"b138d8594deae158dd7023e14aabcd7fa68d466ce8f01e5ecd898962b6f1fecb","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T13:20:18.578Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:20:18.578Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Studio-Canvas is a client/server applications for dynamically rendering the virtual canva